nd what you have to understand  is that with a lot of the individuals  described by the term tang  which again I think we shouldn't use  when you confront them they will say  it's not that I'm defending Stalin it's  that I'm against imperialism for example  I'm against American Empire or  colonialism or something like that but  you can be against any of those things  without apologizing for Stalin or  minimizing what Stalin did and I make no  secret out of the reality that the the  people that are described by the term  tanki even though it's not a term I use  it's not my part of the left I don't  share that much in common with them  other than the fact that I think on  social issues we would probably all be  united but on economics I think we  probably differ pretty significantly on  geopolitics I think we differ pretty  significantly and I do believe that they  hurt the left overall but my advice to  the people there are so-called tanki's  in our audience and again my advice to  the non tanki's is don't use the term  tanki because it is it is an insult I  don't even know I mean is that a term  you're familiar with pat because this is  one of those terms where in certain  circles it's become a big thing but a  lot of people on the sort of mainstream  left of the u.s. aren't even aware of  this debate that's going on yet again  I'm unfamiliar with this term kind of  like with what we discussed before  non-playable characters yeah I guess I'm  just not on those subreddits you know  I'm not in the places where these terms  are used yeah and that's also why I  think we should avoid the term tanki not  only because it is a pejorative and we  want to try to avoid using at homonyms  we want to argue political positions I  also think it's a bad idea to use it  because a lot of people just don't  understand what you're talking about I  think it's much more relevant to talk  about you know I've talked about what I  call a strain of Leninism among the left  right now and it does relate to  positions on Venezuela and Syria and  Russia and taught use more precise  accurate terms that aren't perjorative  and if somebody thinks that Leninist is  pejorative then I think there's probably  a conversation to have there about what  whether words even have value or meaning  anymore because that has a much more  specific definition send me your  thoughts  if you think that the term tanky is not  an ad hominem I also want to hear from  you because I think it's pretty pretty  clear that it is we have a fantastic  bonus show for you today get access to  the bonus show by becoming a member at  WWJ impact muncom or by becoming a  patron at patreon.com slash david pakman  show I'll speak to you then
 

